## Context

Entire records AI coding-agent sessions as git checkpoints. Subagent work becomes a "task record" on the parent session. OpenCode (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/`) is integrated through an embedded TypeScript plugin (`entire_plugin.ts`) that pipes small JSON payloads to `entire hooks opencode <verb>`; `lifecycle.go`'s `ParseHookEvent` turns each verb into an `agent.Event`. OpenCode transcripts live in its SQLite DB, so the adapter fetches them with `opencode export <sessionID>` via `fetchAndCacheExport`, which stages into the shared `.entire` root and returns `.entire/tmp/<sessionID>.json` (under `ENTIRE_TEST_OPENCODE_MOCK_EXPORT` it returns a pre-written file instead); `runOpenCodeExportToFileFn` is the seam tests stub.

OpenCode's `task` tool runs each subagent as a real child session with `parentID`. The plugin (later chunk) will send two new verbs: `subagent-start` when the parent's task part first binds the tool call ID to the child session ID, and `subagent-stop` from `tool.execute.after`. Chunk 1 (already merged on this branch) added `agent.Event.DeferredCompletion` (a SubagentStart that records an in-flight task marker) and made the shared Final capture scan a declared child transcript for `CompletionWithoutLaunch` events unless `SubagentTranscriptUnavailable` is set. Your job is the Go adapter side: parse the two verbs into events with that shape.

